From 4f8d86b1593952acb9beb9b01af2c5b7be40fad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rpc: keep HTTP workers available during long-poll requests

Use complete coroutine dispatch for authenticated JSON-RPC and block/template
long polling. Preserve eCash consensus and ordinary RPC behavior, release chain
locks before suspension, and keep outstanding requests bounded by the existing
workqueue-plus-worker capacity.

Serialize timer initiation and cancellation on one strand to prevent lost wakeups
and concurrent timer mutation. Preserve ABC negative-timeout behavior. Add native
wake/timeout coverage and a one-worker functional regression with seven long
polls, ordinary requests, block notification and shutdown. Existing HTTP, RPC,
authentication and whitelist suites remain unchanged and pass.

Original-Patches: ecash/013, ecash/014, ecash/020
Source-Split-Ids: 14, 16, 17, 35
Candidate-Repair: Reunite the missing HTTP implementation and wait conversions
with their first responsible coroutine feature; retain snapshot reads/templates
as separate later purposes. The unrelated large-request limit belongs with batch
RPC. Before/after timeout evidence and source hashes are recorded in the ledger.

Candidate-Repair: Move the original 50-waiter/four-worker native coroutine regression out of the later snapshot foundation and into the complete coroutine owner. Preserve every assertion and register the standalone suite; no snapshot prerequisite is introduced. Clean replay and gates pending for this amended owner.
